<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Tile Horizontally</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-US">This command is accessible from</span> <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Windows &gt; Tile Horizontally</b></span><span class="Path">,</span> <span lang="EN-US">by pressing</span> <span class="Shortcut" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Ctrl + Alt + H</b></span><span lang="EN-US">,</span> or from the <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>toolbar</b></span>. If <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Tile windows horizontally</b></span> is not selected on the toolbar, hold down the left mouse button on the current selection for a second to show up the drop-down toolbar. Select <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Tile windows horizontally</b></span> button from there.</p>
<p class="description"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Tile Horizontally</span> <span lang="EN-US">is a standard Windows command. It tiles in horizontal direction all open windows.</span></p>
